User Experience Sync

User Experience Sync is a feature for W365 Frontline Cloud PCs in shared mode and W365 Cloud apps.

This cloud-native solution delivers a seamless and consistent experience for users across Cloud PC and Cloud app sessions.

User Experience Sync creates and attaches individual user storage to shared Cloud PCs.

When a user signs in, their individual storage is attached, providing access to their settings, files, and app data.

While creating provisioning policy by selecting "Enable user experience sync" in the configuration section.

Windows 365 Cloud Apps

Windows 365 Cloud apps allow administrators to give users secure access to individual apps hosted on a Cloud PC, without requiring a dedicated Cloud PC for every user.

Windows 365 Cloud apps run on W365 Frontline Cloud PCs in shared mode; W365 Frontline licenses are required to use Cloud apps.

Prerequisites:

To create Cloud apps you need W365 Frontline license.

To create Cloud apps from custom apps that are not available on Gallery image you can use a custom image.

You don't need to create a Provisioning Policy to create a cloud PC using W365 Business. To provision cloud PC you can simply assign the W365 Business license to the user.

You don't need an Azure subscription because everything works with Azure AD natively.

Provisioning Policy can take up to 24 hours for creating cloud PCs.

